  "notes": "Things on the road past the grey doors to look at, and go on looking at. The road is one short scene passed over and over, more worn each pass, and more likely to break. src/data/source-outskirts-arrival.js gives a piece an `inspect` key; main.js picks the node: the key the first time, `-again` after that, `-far` when it is found further down the road (pass 15 and on), and the errand steps by flag. Two errands pay out a little composure, once each (a choice's `reward` and `rewardId`): the ledger read at three different lodges and signed, and the return half of a ticket found in the van and given back. Three go nowhere on purpose: the timetable, the lodge phone, the guard's name. Lines are his or the direction's; nobody out here explains the road. LOSING HIMSELF (docs/plans/outskirts-losing-himself.md): after the loop pass, her traces become his: the take sheet on the gate, the track sheet on the dash, the bin, the bench slate, the car plate, his name in the ledger (ledger-him, pass 15 on), his coat on the shelter (coat, pass 12 on). The woman is nobody.",
